card.statement:
Let $L=(l_{ij})$ and $\sm=\sm_L$. Let $V$ be a Gelfand-Tsetlin module with $V_{\sm}\neq 0$ and $v\in V_{\sm}$ a nonzero element such that $\sm v=0$. Then the following hold.

- [(i)] $[c_m(x), b_l(y)] V_{\sm}= 0$ for all $x$, $y$ if $l\neq m$;

- [(ii)] $[s_m(x), s_l(y)] V_{\sm}= 0$ or all $x$, $y$, $s\in \{b, c\}$ if $|l -m| \neq 1$;

- [(iii)] $[c_m(-l_{mi}), b_m(-l_{mj})]v=0$ if $l_{mi}\neq l_{mj}$;

- [(iv)] $b_m(-l_{mi}+1)c_m(-l_{mi}) v= - a_{m+1}(-l_{mi}+1)a_{m-1}(-l_{mi})v$;

- [(v)] $
c_m(-l_{mi}-1)b_m(-l_{mi})v= - a_{m+1}(-l_{mi})a_{m-1}(-l_{mi}-1)v$;

- [(vi)] $(x - y)  [a_m(x), c_m(y)] w= c_m(x)a_m(y)w - c_m(y)a_m(x)w$ for any $w\in V_{\sm}$;

- [(vii)] $(x - y)  [a_m(x), b_m(y)] w=- b_m(x)a_m(y) w+ b_m(y)a_m(x)w$ for any $w\in V_{\sm}$.
